review_comments.body:
`datetime.fromtimestamp()` can raise `OverflowError` (for values outside platform `time_t` range) or `OSError` on some platforms. The rest of `_parse_timestamp` promises to never break `get_info()` by returning `None` on failure, but this branch can still propagate an exception if the API returns an unusually large/small numeric timestamp.

Consider wrapping in try/except consistent with the string branch:
```python
if isinstance(value, (int, float)):
    try:
        return datetime.fromtimestamp(value, tz=timezone.utc)
    except (ValueError, OverflowError, OSError):
        return None
```

