review_comments.body:
**Medium: Head-of-line blocking — a slow delivery blocks all subsequent events**

The spawned task processes `Command::Deliver` sequentially. With `max_retries=3` and `request_timeout_secs=10`, a single failing delivery can take ~47 seconds (4 attempts × 10s + backoff sleeps), during which all other events for this endpoint queue up behind it.

If ordering guarantees are not required within an endpoint, spawn each delivery as its own task:

```rust
Command::Deliver(event) => {
    tokio::spawn(deliver(client.clone(), config.clone(), signer.clone(), event));
}
```

If ordering is needed, consider a `Semaphore` to allow bounded concurrency (e.g., 4 in-flight) while preserving ordering within each batch.

