review_comments.body:
**Medium: HMAC signature and timestamp are static across all retry attempts**

The signature + timestamp pair is computed once (line 108) before the retry loop, then reused verbatim on every attempt. An attacker who observes any single attempt (whether initial or retry) can replay it within the 300-second freshness window, and the receiver cannot distinguish a legitimate retry from a replay.

Recommendation: move the signed-headers computation inside the retry loop with a fresh timestamp per attempt:

```rust
for attempt in 0..=config.max_retries {
    let signed_headers = signer.as_ref().map(|signer| {
        let timestamp = SystemTime::now()
            .duration_since(UNIX_EPOCH)
            .unwrap_or_default()
            .as_secs()
            .to_string();
        // ... rest of signing ...
    });
    // ... build request ...
}
```

