review_comments.body:
**Deterministic retry backoff causes thundering herd**

The pure exponential backoff has no jitter. When a webhook endpoint becomes unavailable, all in-flight events retry at exactly the same wall-clock times, amplifying load on the recovering service. Add ±25% random jitter:

```rust
let jitter = Duration::from_millis(rand::thread_rng().gen_range(0..base.min(1000)));
tokio::time::sleep(base_dur + jitter).await;
```

