review_comments.body:
**`Some("")` passes validation but downstream in `deliver_to_endpoint` (http.rs:144) it's filtered with `.filter(|secret| !secret.is_empty())`. This inconsistency means two semantically identical values (`None` and `Some("")`) travel different code paths.**

Consider normalizing to `None` at the deserialization boundary:

```rust
match secret {
    Some(value) if !value.is_empty() && value.len() < 16 => {
        Err(D::Error::custom("webhook secret must be at least 16 bytes"))
    }
    Some(value) if value.is_empty() => Ok(None),
    other => Ok(other),
}
```

This eliminates the downstream filter in `deliver_to_endpoint` and avoids a future trap where someone adds `secret.is_some()` and gets unexpected behavior with an empty string.

