review_comments.body:
**`flush()` has no timeout — can block shutdown indefinitely**

If an endpoint worker is stuck in a retry loop (e.g., waiting on a 5s `reqwest` timeout + backoff), `flush()` will await the `oneshot::Receiver` until the retry loop completes and processes the Flush message. This blocks graceful shutdown for up to 5s × (retries+1) per stuck endpoint.

Add a timeout to protect shutdown:

```rust
for reply in replies {
    let _ = tokio::time::timeout(Duration::from_secs(10), reply).await;
}
```

