review_comments.body:
**Performance: `payload.to_vec()` and `signature()` are recomputed on every retry attempt**

The body bytes (`payload.to_vec()`) and the HMAC signature are re-derived on each retry iteration (lines 123, 129). Both are pure functions of immutable inputs — pre-compute them once before the loop:

```rust
let body = payload.to_vec();
let sig_header = endpoint.secret.as_deref()
    .filter(|s| !s.is_empty())
    .map(|secret| signature(secret, payload));

for attempt in 0..=config.max_retries {
    let mut request = client.post(endpoint.url.as_str())
        .header("content-type", "application/json")
        .header("x-cube-event", event.event.as_str())
        .header("x-cube-timestamp", event.timestamp.to_rfc3339())
        .body(body.clone());  // cheap Bytes ref-count bump with reqwest's Bytes
    if let Some(ref sig) = sig_header {
        request = request.header("x-cube-signature-256", sig.as_str());
    }
    // …
}
```

Switching from `Vec<u8>` to `bytes::Bytes` (which reqwest accepts natively) would make `.clone()` a reference-count bump instead of a full copy.

